# Documentation Sync

## Sync Points

1. After `phase-executor` — Status / Notes / changed files / risks / next phase.
2. After `test-runner` — verification, coverage, residual risk; link report; may set `Verified`.

After sync point 2 marks **`Verified`**, the **parent agent** commits the phase. Push / stacked PR
**only when the user asks**.

## What `doc-sync` May Update

- Phase **Status** and **Notes**
- Links to test reports and ADRs

## What `doc-sync` Must Not Do

- Modify product code or tests
- Invent evidence
- Create new SDDs or test reports
- Overwrite `PR` cells

## Evidence

- `Verified` requires `docs/sdd/test-reports/` path with command evidence
- `Implemented` should list changed files

## File Ownership

| File | Creates | Updates |
|---|---|---|
| `docs/sdd/<slug>.md` | architect-planner | doc-sync (Status/Notes); parent (`PR`) |
| `docs/sdd/test-reports/<slug>.md` | test-runner | test-runner |
| `docs/investigation/<slug>.md` | code-investigator | code-investigator |
| `docs/adr/NNNN-*.md` | architect-planner / rule-feedback-writer | same |
